# G1: the first attach with ALL FIVE levers on, on the TIMED profile (c2-packed-tp4-speed-vglue: c2-packed-tp4-speed, the verify's
# T1 and T2 audits OFF, the drafter's K/V slide ON, QWEN_FAST_TP4_COMMIT_LANES / _SHARD_VALUES / _GDN_GLUE / _GDN_BLOCK_CONV /
# _ATTN_FOLD = 1). An all-four reset, then the smoke of a warmup, one coding stream and the mixed four-stream test (concurrent4).
# This is the cheap run that puts the new launches on a card for the first time: the half-tile row mover (gdn_rows_dma_tp) for the
# split, the canon block, the window stack, the unstack and the merge; ttnn.gather on the row-major logits; gdn_decode_conv_gates at
# batch 64 over the block (the op's own validation admits it, but it has never been called with more than 32 rows on a card); the
# block attention fold; the eight-lane commit. It proves the levers ENGAGE and that the texts are coherent; it does not prove them
# exact (G2 does, on the audited profile). It is also the timed arm: the live-4 round, the verify span and the commit phase are read
# here, against the S3a-era profile numbers (trace 0 at live-4: verify 61.8 ms of device span, 57.5 ms of kernels; round 124.5 ms
# at tau 5.1; GDN commits 4 x 0.65 ms; the sampler 1.73 ms; GDN glue 6.07 ms; attention glue, prep and K/V write 5.7 ms; SDPA 7.12 ms).
# Projection to confirm or refute (all five, every saving an estimate from that profile, nothing run on a card): verify about 50 ms
# (-11.6 ms: V2 -4.7, V1 -3.8, V3a -2.3, V4a -0.8; C1a -1.8 to -2.1 is commit time outside the trace, so -13.4 ms per round; the extra DMA launches of V2 and V1 are not netted out), a live-4 round of about 111 ms, about 46 tok/s per
# user at tau 5.1. If a lever fell back, its saving is absent: read the markers first.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card verify-glue window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/vglue and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here
# names a rig, a card or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The window's jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed
# from this branch.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image G0 builds from this same commit; a later commit needs a new tag.
# C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-vglue-1 is a PLACEHOLDER: set it (in every template of the window) to the tag the driver of the window picks, once
# the image is built from the pushed branch.
# The markers to read (scripts/ci/tp4_vglue.py): '[PINDIAG] tp4 vglue engaged site=packed_verify levers=<list> attn_fold=16
# gdn_glue=48 gdn_merge=48 gdn_block_conv=48 shard_values=1' once per captured verify trace (the counts are per layer: 16 attention
# layers, 48 GDN layers; a lever that fell back shows its own *_fallback count instead), '[PINDIAG] tp4 vglue engaged site=commit
# lanes=<workers per layer x layers> chips=4' once, and '[PINDIAG] tp4 vglue engaged site=sampler shard_values=1' once.
# '[PINDIAG] tp4 vglue fell back site=<split|merge|block_conv|attention|sampler> reason=...' is a lever declining (its served path
# ran instead): read every one before trusting a timing, because a fallen-back lever saves nothing. Any '[PINDIAG] tp4 vglue audit
# mismatch' line fails the smoke and the gate by itself (c2_smoke_check's 'audit mismatch' rule).
# Duration (estimate): reset 1-3 min; the first engine build 10-30 min (kernel compile on a cold cache: the row mover, the lanes
# commit and the block fold are generic_op sources, compiled at first use, 0.1-2 s each); the three tests 8-15 min: 20 / 35 / 90 min
# (a collective hang runs the 80-min ready loop, then the reset).
# Read: the ready line; the launched-argv line (profile c2-packed-tp4-speed-vglue, QWEN_FAST_TP=4 and the five flags); no attach
# refusal; the markers above, every count at its full value; [PACKED-PHASE] (verify: input, trace, sync, readback; commits; early
# draft; gap) and [PACKED-PUBLISH] per round, medians at 4 live, against the speed window's K2 (verify 63.3, four serial commits
# 37.9, round 170 at two ramp users); readback_ms; the coding decode_tok_s; the concurrent4 per-user decode_tok_s and the [ACCEPT]
# mean.
# STOP on an attach refusal, a hang, garbage text, an errored or empty stream, an audit mismatch line, or any vglue fell-back line:
# a fallen-back lever means the window is not measuring what it says. The smoke step enforces the first four (c2_smoke_check.py); the
# fell-back lines are read here.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-vglue-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-speed-vglue
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent4
